# ===========================================
# Pharmacy OS Backend - Environment Variables
#
# Local:  copy to .env and fill in.
# RunxBuild (or any Docker PaaS): paste these key/value pairs into the
#   service's Environment Variables / Secrets panel (encrypted at rest).
#
# Startup FAILS on purpose when APP_ENV=production and any of
# CORS_ORIGINS / PUBLIC_APP_URL / BOOTSTRAP_SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL is missing
# (see config.Validate) — treat that list as the production checklist.
# ===========================================

# -------------------------------------------
# Server
# -------------------------------------------
# RunxBuild injects PORT automatically — never set it manually there.
# Resolution order in code: PORT > BACKEND_PORT > 8080.
#PORT=8080
#BACKEND_PORT=8080
APP_ENV=development            # development | staging | production
LOG_LEVEL=info                 # debug | info | warn | error
# Leave APP_DEBUG unset in production: "true" exposes debug-only schema
# endpoints (debug_schema_handler.go).
#APP_DEBUG=true

# -------------------------------------------
# Database — DockHosting managed PostgreSQL (PRIMARY)
# -------------------------------------------
# Postgres 16/15/14, provisioned from the DockHosting dashboard
# (Databases → New database). Docs: docs/deployment.md §11.
#
# The app runs on RunxBuild = OUTSIDE DockHosting, so the private network
# is not an option. Use the PUBLIC path:
#   1. Database → Public access → switch ON (a dedicated port is assigned)
#   2. Database → Firewall → allow-list the RunxBuild egress IPs
#      (with no rules the port is reachable from anywhere)
#   3. Copy host/port/user/password from the Public access tab:
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://<user>:<password>@<host>:<public-port>/<dbname>?sslmode=require&pool_max_conns=10
#
# The public endpoint is TLS-encrypted; sslmode=require is mandatory.
# pgx pools long-lived connections, so the TLS handshake cost is paid per
# pooled connection, not per query.
#
# If the backend ever runs ON DockHosting itself, attach the database to
# the project and use the injected PRIVATE connection string instead
# (faster, zero public exposure).
#
# ALTERNATIVE — Supabase (session pooler, port 5432, IPv4-friendly):
#   postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=require&pool_max_conns=10
# (transaction pooler = port 6543, also works — prepared statements are
# already disabled in cmd/server/main.go)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/postgres

# -------------------------------------------
# River Queue (Postgres-based job queue) — RESERVED
# -------------------------------------------
# The current binary does NOT run River workers yet (internal/jobs is a
# stub). Keep RIVER_DSN identical to DATABASE_URL so future activation
# needs no config change.
RIVER_DSN=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/postgres

# -------------------------------------------
# Authentication (Go-managed; HTTP-only cookies)
# -------------------------------------------
# APP_ENV=production forces Secure cookies automatically.
AUTH_COOKIE_SECURE=false
# Keep EMPTY when frontend and API live on different hosts.
AUTH_COOKIE_DOMAIN=

# -------------------------------------------
# Brevo transactional email (OTP, password reset,
# support quiet-hours alerts)
# -------------------------------------------
BREVO_API_KEY=
MAIL_FROM_EMAIL=               # verified Brevo sender, e.g. no-reply@your-domain
MAIL_FROM_NAME=Pharmacy OS
PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000   # pharmacy frontend base URL (reset links)
# Dedicated inbox for support quiet-hours notifications (§9.2 of
# deployment.md). Falls back to MAIL_FROM_EMAIL when empty.
PLATFORM_SUPPORT_EMAIL=

# -------------------------------------------
# CORS & request limits
# -------------------------------------------
# Exact origins, comma-separated, no trailing slashes, no wildcards.
# Must list EVERY frontend origin that calls the API with cookies
# (this also feeds the support WebSocket origin check).
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:3001
MAX_REQUEST_SIZE=10485760      # bytes (default 10MB)

# -------------------------------------------
# First platform administrator (bootstrap)
# -------------------------------------------
# Runs on every startup, idempotent. MANDATORY in production:
# BOOTSTRAP_SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL is required or the server refuses to start.
BOOTSTRAP_SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL=
BOOTSTRAP_SUPER_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
BOOTSTRAP_SUPER_ADMIN_FIRST_NAME=Mohamed
BOOTSTRAP_SUPER_ADMIN_LAST_NAME=Admin
BOOTSTRAP_SUPER_ADMIN_COMPANY=Pharmacy OS

# -------------------------------------------
# XPay — the ACTIVE payment gateway (Phase X)
# -------------------------------------------
# All three keys below together activate XPay checkout (config.XPayEnabled).
# Omit them to fall back to Paymob, or to manual payments.
XPAY_SECRET_KEY=               # sk_test_* / sk_live_*  (server-only)
XPAY_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=          # pk_test_* / pk_live_*  (browser SDK)
XPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=           # whsec_* from the webhook endpoint
XPAY_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=            # random token appended to the webhook URL (?token=…)
#XPAY_BASE_URL=https://api.xpay.app

# -------------------------------------------
# Paymob — previous gateway (optional fallback, Phase G)
# -------------------------------------------
# Paymob checkout activates when the four required values are present and
# XPay is absent. Secrets stay server-side only.
PAYMOB_SECRET_KEY=             # dashboard "Secret Key" (legacy name PAYMOB_API_KEY also works)
PAYMOB_PUBLIC_KEY=             # pk_… for the Unified Checkout iframe
PAYMOB_CARD_INTEGRATION_ID=    # numeric Online Card integration ID
PAYMOB_WALLET_INTEGRATION_ID=  # numeric Mobile Wallets integration ID (optional)
PAYMOB_HMAC_SECRET=            # HMAC-SHA512 webhook verification
PAYMOB_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=          # random token appended to the webhook URL (?token=…)
#PAYMOB_BASE_URL=https://accept.paymob.com
#PAYMOB_DIAG_API_KEY=          # optional: enables the delivery-diagnostics endpoint
